WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.190
- Last time you we were here we talked

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:02.712
about your farm and it's
in the middle of nowhere.

00:00:02.712 --> 00:00:03.545
- Yes.

00:00:03.545 --> 00:00:04.378
- I love middle of nowhere.

00:00:04.378 --> 00:00:05.211
That's where my ranch is.

00:00:05.211 --> 00:00:06.044
I think it's amazing.

00:00:06.044 --> 00:00:06.877
So how are things?

00:00:06.877 --> 00:00:07.710
- No, they're, it's fine.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.670
I mean, listen, it's winter time.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:12.090
Yesterday it was 61 when I left,

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:13.670
tomorrow there's gonna be a foot of snow.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:15.150
So the problem is

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.400
if there's wind and ice, the whole,

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.270
everything shuts down.

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.530
Nobody gets power and
we have two generators.

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:22.740
I am a lucky person.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:23.780
We have two generators

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:25.780
and our one generator just blew,

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.490
two weeks ago with a huge ice storm.

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:29.706
I mean, you couldn't
even leave your house.

00:00:29.706 --> 00:00:30.539
- Yeah.

00:00:30.539 --> 00:00:31.840
- I just have two small kids

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.820
and in the middle of the
night have to have no heat.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.000
Like we ended up having
to like walk outside

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.870
in five degree weather to
the barn and sleep there,

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:42.410
because we had a, the generator ran

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:44.590
for that 'cause it runs
for the horse barn.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:45.423
- Yeah.

00:00:45.423 --> 00:00:46.675
- And then the extra guest
barn and the house...

00:00:46.675 --> 00:00:47.750
- So the animals were good.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:48.824
Y'all were just cold.

00:00:48.824 --> 00:00:49.657
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:49.657 --> 00:00:50.490
- No, the animals are fine.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:51.670
They're like, it's just,
there's like a cat room

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:52.760
where the cat lives and you know,

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.210
the cat at night goes in

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.490
and you have warmth for that

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:56.640
and water and running water.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:57.600
So we were fine.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.570
We were, we're very
lucky, but it was like one

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:00.910
of those things where like, I,

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:01.910
this is what you do.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:02.930
This is what you gave up.

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:07.620
You sacrifice these
things when nature happens

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:08.453
you know what I mean?

00:01:08.453 --> 00:01:09.410
And it's just..

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:10.418
- I love it.

00:01:10.418 --> 00:01:11.251
Do you love it?

00:01:11.251 --> 00:01:14.153
- The, no one running
water situation is like,

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.490
it'll kill me.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:18.155
- It'll...( Kelly laughing)

00:01:18.155 --> 00:01:18.988
(audience laughs)

00:01:18.988 --> 00:01:21.180
- 2:30 a.m in the morning walking

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.660
with my one and a half
year old trying to wake up,

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:26.010
and my five year old
was like what an irony,

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:28.490
on I it was just like, no thanks.

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:29.790
But I really love my farm.

